 ## MVP Scope
 
@@ -98,7 +98,34 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); AuthZ stays out of scope per #20 and HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (exactly-once; the caller must hold the `call` ability on the ticket's queue — see [Queue management and call access](#queue-management-and-call-access)). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields. Deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) is implemented by `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` with the three call-panel modes below (`any` applies fairness; `priority_only`/`normal_only` ignore it); both paths enforce the `call` ability, and HTTP/Livewire panels remain future work.
+
+### Queue management and call access
+
+Authorization is decided in one place, `App\Policies\QueuePolicy`:
+
+| Ability | Who |
+| ------- | --- |
+| `create` (argument: the entity), `update`, `manageAccess` | Owner/admin of the queue's entity. Employees, members of other entities and non-members are denied. |
+| `call` | Owner/admin of the queue's entity **always** (no grant needed). An employee **only** with a `queue_access` row for **that** queue whose `permissions` is an array containing `call` (a corrupted, non-array value denies). Everyone else is denied. |
+
+**Queue lifecycle** (owner/admin only; others get `AuthorizationException` and nothing is written):
+
+- `App\Actions\CreateQueue` — name is trimmed (1–255 chars); the slug defaults to `Str::slug(name)` and an explicit slug is slugified too (`Atendimento Geral` → `atendimento-geral`). New queues are active.
+- `App\Actions\UpdateQueue` — any combination of name, slug and `isActive`; `null` leaves a field unchanged. Keeping the queue's own slug is fine.
+- Slugs are unique **within an entity** (the same slug may exist in another entity). A duplicate — including one caught by the DB unique index in a race — is a `ValidationException`.
+- **No hard delete.** A queue is retired by deactivating it (`is_active = false`): its tickets are kept and issuing or calling on it keeps failing with `InactiveQueueException`. There is deliberately no delete/remove/destroy queue action.
+
+**Per-queue access grants** — `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess` (owner/admin only; an employee cannot grant themselves access):
+
+- The only permission today is `call` (`App\Enums\QueuePermission`). Unknown strings or non-string entries are a `ValidationException` and nothing is stored.
+- A non-empty list upserts the `queue_access` row of the membership on the queue; an empty list revokes (deletes) it. The membership and the queue must belong to the same entity (`ValidationException` otherwise).
+- Every grant and every effective revoke is written to the `audit` log channel as `queue.access.granted` / `queue.access.revoked` with `actor_id`, `queue_id`, `entity_membership_id` (and the stored `permissions`). Revoking when there was no row logs nothing.
+
+**Where `call` is enforced:**
+
+- `CallNextTicket` (every call mode): lock the queue, reject inactive queues (`InactiveQueueException`), then authorize (`AuthorizationException`, no ticket changes), then pick the ticket.
+- `Ticket::call()`: lock the queue, reject inactive queues (`InactiveQueueException`), then authorize (`AuthorizationException`, even when the ticket was already called), then require a waiting ticket (`LogicException`).
 
 ### Priority
 
